ed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a oriented lumpectomy specimen which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  There is one needle localization wire in place  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is cut along its long axis from medial to lateral to reveal a cut surface consisting of an ill defined white gray relatively firm mass with two areas of gross hemorrhage  The greatest dimensions of the mass are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The mass grossly abuts the superior posterior margins  The mass is 0 3cm and 0 2cm from the inferior and anterior margins  The specimen submitted in cassettes A J  from medial to lateral  The specimen is submitted from medial to lateral in representative sections  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast anterior  medial  superior  inferior margin  stitch at true margin   is an irregular fragment of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  There is a suture to denote the true margin  The true margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes K O  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast superior lateral margin  stitch at true margin   is an irregular fragment of fibroadipose tissue which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  There is