ents are serially sectioned and submitted entirely but separately in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   respectively  Received fresh and labeled  final margin  superior   is a single unoriented fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh and labeled  final margin  lateral   is a single unoriented fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh and labeled  final margin  inferior   are 3 unoriented fragments of fibrofatty breast tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  All the fragments are serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab    labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right sentinel node  hot and blue   261   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue which is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink lymph node which is bisected and entirely submitted for Frozen Section as FX  1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT SENTINEL NODE  HOT   BLUE   261   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday May 20   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 08 02PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Rare tumor cells stain for est