Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 13 CLINICAL DATA  74 y o  female with breast carcinoma by fine needle aspiration undergoing right modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVASING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 7 OF 8 LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY SOFT TISSUE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SPECIMEN  1   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 5 OF 5 LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY VEINS  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tissue fragment with a 0 8cm firm lymph node  The node is sectioned to reveal a white tan  firm cut surface  Half the node is frozen as FX 1  and saved frozen  The remainder is submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  additional axillary nodes  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of adipose tissue from which lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes B through C  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  right modified radical mastectomy   is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x 22 x 4 5cm  with an attached axilla of  14 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0 cm and an overlying skin ellipse measuring  23 x 11cm   containing an eccentric nipple  4 0cm in diameter  7 7cm away from the medial end of the skin ellipse  The nipple areola complex is grossly unremarkable  No scars are grossly identified in the overlying skin ellipse  The deep resection margin consist of a smooth fascial plane  The specimen is inked black and the axillary contents are removed  A lymph node dissection is performed  The main mastectomy specimen is then serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  gritty area with a stellate border that comes to within 0 8cm of the deep  closest  margin  The inferior margin is 2 0cm away  and the superior margin is 2 5cm away from the mass  SECTION CODE  D L  Axillary lymph nodes  M  Mass  in relation to deep margin  N  Closest inferior margin  O  Deep margin  P Q  Representative sections of tumor nodules  R  Representative section of normal breast parenchyma away from mass lesion  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS 1  LYMPH NODE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART B  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
