  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Seven specimens are received  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm incision of breast biopsy with long suture designating lateral and short suture designating superior aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  Inferior is yellow  superior is red  lateral is blue  medial is green  anterior and posterior are black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm stellate gritty mass present at the anterior margin and 0 2cm from the posterior margin  0 5cm from the lateral margin  Mass is submitted in cassettes A through C with anterior  black   lateral  blue   and posterior  black overinked in yellow   Needle localization site  slightly firm no gross tumor  and anterior margin are submitted in D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are the 6 remaining specimens  Labeled as  left breast  additional anterior medial margin  is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with focal fibrocystic changes  submitted entirely in cassettes E through J  Labeled as  left breast  final shaved margins  are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  They are inked and sectioned to reveal fibroadipose tissue with focal cystic changes  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes K  L and M  Labeled as  left axillary contents  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are extracted  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 7cm in greatest dimension  submitted in N through S  Labeled as  reexcision  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse containing a 4 8cm well healed  linear scar  There is a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  and a short stitch designating the superior aspect which is inked in blue  while the inferior aspect is inked in black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with an associated area of stellate fibrosis measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and extending to the superior and inferior margins  Posterior to the biopsy cavity is a rubbery  tan white  nodular mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and present at superior  inferior and posterior margins  The biopsy cavity itself is 0 2cm from the nearest  inferior  margin  Section code  T W  Biopsy cavity  nearest margin in W  lateral to medial X Y  Adjacent fibrous areas Z  Uninvolved parenchyma Designated right axillary contents is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which several node like structures have been extracted ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension and submitted in cassettes