Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 13 CLINICAL DATA  History of left breast ca  Status post left mastectomy  A right breast mass biopsy showed intraductal carcinoma extending to within 2mm of surgical margin  Now for right mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY CAVITY WITH GRANULATION TISSUE  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELLS  AND FAT NECROSIS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE INCLUDING APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND DUCTAL DILATATION  PAPILLARY HYPERPLASIA  ATYPICAL HYPERPLASIA  MIXED DUCTAL AND LOBULAR TYPES   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 37                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right  is a 28cm long  right mastectomy with axillary tail of the breast attached  The breast tissue measures 20 x 24 x 3cm with a 17 x 4 5cm skin ellipse  A 3cm healing scar is present in the outer lower quadrant  abutting the areolar at 45 degrees  An older puckered 1cm in length scar is present in the medial inferior section of the skin ellipse  3 5cm from the nipple  The nipple and areolar are grossly unremarkable  The axillary tail of the breast measures 10 x 6 x 0 5cm   Assuming this to be axillary tail  allows me to orient the specimen with regard to medial  lateral  superior and inferior   The specimen is inked black with a strip of red ink superiorly along the ellipse and sectioned to reveal the recent biopsy cavity 2cm deep to the healing incision scar  and 2 5cm from the deep margin  The cavity measures 0 4cm in diameter and is surrounded by white fibrous tissue  and numerous  yellow specks suspicious for fat necrosis  measuring up to 0 3cm in diameter  2cm medial to the biopsy cavity is a 3 x 1 x 0 5cm area of white fibrous tissue  with punctate hemorrhages interspersed among the tissue  This area is not grossly suspicious for carcinoma  This tissue is 2cm deep to the skin ellipse  and 5cm from the nearest margin  that being the deep margin  Located 10cm medial and 3 5cm from the deep superior margin is a 0 3cm hard  tan nodule with associated fibrous tissue  Dense fibrous tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1cm in dimension is present at the medial deep margin  Section Code  A E  biopsy cavity and surrounding breast tissue  representative sections  F  deep margin  the closest margin to the biopsy cavity  representative section  G H  fibrous tissue located 3cm lateral to the biopsy cavity  representative sections  I  fibrous tissue  the medial deep margin  J  tissue lateral and adjacent to the biopsy cavity  representative sections  K  fibrous tissue posterior to the biopsy cavity  representative sections  L  nipple from the trisected end  M  representative sections of areolar and deep tissue  representative sections  N  recent scar  cross section  representative section  O  distant scar  cross section  representative section  P Q  representative tissue 2cm from the posterior deep margin  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MEEI INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART    RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 10 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3 OF 3  EXTENDING TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  WITH METASTASIS TO AN INTRA PARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODE  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  In situ carcinoma is not identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptor status will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm nodule of breast tissue with a well demarcated  irregular firm and gritty white to gray nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm in size abutting an inked resection margin  A portion of the suspicious nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  submitted entirely in A through I  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
