ainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of yellow adipose tissue and white fibrous tissue  with focal cysts  No lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Ill defined gritty nodular area in the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section outer lower quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Areola to subareolar tissue  radial sections  Received fresh  labeled  right breast skin   are 2 irregular portions of skin  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND  1A   RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN 1 LYMPH NODE AND NO CANCER PRESENT IN BREAST PARENCHYMA  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 15 30PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cel