Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  31 AUG 98 at 10 42 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  REMOVED_DATE CM  MIXED MODERATELY AND POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MIXED HIGH AND INTERMEDIATE GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Definite angiolymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The moderately differentiated tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The moderately differentiated tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The poorly differentiated tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  Rare poorly differentiated tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also