ich are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of gray white to tan red fibrofatty tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  inferior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm portion of dense gray white fibrous tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a homogeneous dense gray white fibrous cut surface with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  posterior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of gray white to tan yellow fibrofatty tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal diffuse dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm portion of gray white to tan yellow fibrofatty tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focally dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   SENTINEL NODE  RIGHT BREAST   NO CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cel