argins measure REMOVED_DATE  cm or greater   STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID        GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received are 2 containers which are each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN       Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm  mastectomy  specimen with a short suture designating the superior  a long suture  designating the lateral and an extra stitch designating axillary tail  The  overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm nipple and areola appear unremarkable  The anterior  margin of the specimen is inked blue  the posterior margin is inked black  The  specimen consists of yellow white  fibrofatty tissue with focal hemorrhagic  areas and nodular areas  Four possible lymph nodes are identified in the  lateral tissue  Also received within the container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  aggregate of unremarkable pieces of fibroadipose tissue  The following  representative sections are submitted      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative upper outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative upper inner quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative lower inner quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative lower outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative central breast    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 possible lymph nodes    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of additional pieces of fat     Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm  mastectomy  specimen with a short suture designating the superior  a long suture  designating the lateral and an extra stitch designating axillary tail  The  overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm nipple and areola appear unremarkable  The anterior  margin of the specimen is inked blue  and the posterior margin is inked black   The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm ill defined  stellate  white  indurated area within the central outer aspect of the breast  subjacent to the  lateral 