Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 10 CLINICAL DATA  Mammo densities on both breasts                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE SUPERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  AND WITHIN LESS THAT REMOVED_DATE CM OF OTHER RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MODERATE GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS AND PRESENT AT RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No blood vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MICROCALCIFICATIONS AND MICROCYSTS THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 10                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 3cm irregular  firm and gritty nodule in the center of the specimen  approximately 0 3cm from the posterior margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in Cassettes A G  with the nodule in Cassettes A C  the superior margin Cassette D  and the inferior margin in Cassette E  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of breast  with unremarkable yellow fatty cut surface  No discrete lesion is grossly identified  The specimen is submitted entirely in Cassette H L  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  NO GROSS LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GROSS SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  BREAST  LEFT  A REMOVED_DATE CM NODULE HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
