ing of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lesion   is an REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast fragment with a long stitch designating superior aspects and a short stitch designating inferior aspects and a wire designating the antero lateral aspects  The specimen is inked  then sectioned along the needle localization wire to reveal an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm white mass  coming to within than less than 0 1cm of the anteromedial resection margin  This is frozen as FX  1 and FX  2  and resubmitted in cassettes A and B  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  and  left breast margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch indicating the former closest margin  opposite to which is the new margin  this is inked black and a representative radial section is frozen as FX  3 and now resubmitted in C  The remainder of the specimen is inked in blue where the stitch is and black  on the opposite side  sectioned and submitted serially  Further identified as left axillary contents is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm piece of fatty  nodular tissue  with a suture designating the highest node  Section Code  D E  additional sections of main fragment through antero medial aspects adjacent to tip of needle  Further sections reveal a tan  fibrous area located deep  medially REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  F  representative sections through tan  fibrous area of main fragment  G O  remainder of  margin  specimen serially submitted P  highest node Q V  lymph nodes  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 AND  2   LEFT BREAST LESION   INVASIVE DUCTAL AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  TUMOR PRESENT AT ANTERIOR MEDIAL INKED MARGINS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  3   LEFT BREAST MARGIN   NO TUMOR IS SEEN IN PERPENDICULAR SECTIONS FROM NEW MARGIN  O R  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  LESION PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
