Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 14 CLINICAL DATA  80 year old female with breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE CELLULAR MUCINOUS CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of carcinoma  The tumor displays endocrine characteristics  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm simple mastectomy specimen containing a REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm unremarkable skin ellipse with an unremarkable centrally placed nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  gritty  tan tissue mass that extends up to the overlying skin ellipse and to within 0 8cm of the nearest deep margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  No axillary tail is present  Section code  A  tumor with closest deep margin  representative section B  skin with tumor  representative section C F tumor  representative sections G  nipple  trisected  in entirety H  unremarkable parenchyma  representative sections Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  COMP  BREAST HEALTH CENTER REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
