sest to the tumor  is inked in blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal gray white to focally tan  firm tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes I through L  Labeled  left breast final posterior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm portion of breast tissue which is externally unremarkable  A stitch marks the edge which was furthest from the tumor  The surface which was furthest from the tumor is inked in black  and the opposite surface  which was closest to the tumor  is inked in blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable yellow  fibrofatty breast tissue  It is submitted entirely in cassettes M through Q  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Christopher Lee Forthman  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL  EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN PART D  BREAST  LEFT  POSTERIOR FINAL MARGIN   report_end  , Unchecked.
