adical mastectomy specimen consists of a left breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm  an overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 12 5cm  axillary fat tissue REMOVED_DATE x 7 6cm  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm piece of skeletal muscle  There is no cutaneous incision visible  nor is there a nipple or areola present  On the cutaneous surface there is an ulcer measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm  It is yellow  and hemorrhagic with red yellow rolled edges  It is 9 2cm from the lateral skin margin  6 2cm from the medial skin margin  3 2cm from the superior skin margin  and 4 5cm from the inferior skin margin  Lateral and inferior to the ulcer there is a small yellow firm lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The skin surrounding the ulcer is violaceous and mottled  Within the parenchyma there is a firm  white  ill defined mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm  The axillary portion is dissected for lymph nodes  however none are found  Section Code  A  frozen section  1  medial   B  frozen section  2  lateral   C  frozen section  3  superior   D  frozen section  4  inferior   E G  inferior portion of axilla from the left breast  H J  middle third axilla from the left breast  K N  superior portion of axilla from the left breast  O Q  inferior region of axilla of the right breast  R S  largest node in the middle axilla of the right breast  T  external portion of the large node in the right breast  U W  superior axilla from the right breast  X  right nipple  en face  Y  skin papule from the right breast  Z  right nipple  radial section  AA  closest deep margin of the right breast  BB  closest inferior margin of the right breast  CC FF  four representative sections of the mass biopsy cavity  GG  cyst  representative section of the right breast  HH  parenchyma of the right breast behind the nipple  II JJ  parenchyma of the right breast  KK  skin of biopsy cavity  right breast  LL  closest deep margin of the left breast  MM PP  representative sections of the mass  left breast  QQ  grossly normal parenchyma  left breast  RR  ulcerative skin surface with deep tissue  left breast  SS  ulcerative skin area  left breast  TT  skin away from ulcer  left breast  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 4  RIGHT BREAST SKIN MARGIN   RADIATION CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  Horace C  Wu  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST SKIN MARGIN MEDIAL PART B  LATERAL PART C  SUPERIOR PART D  INFERIOR PART E  BREAST  RIGHT  PART F  BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 13 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3   EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INKED DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  AND WITH BLOOD VASCULAR  VENOUS  INVASION   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE TO HIGH PRESENT IN 5 OF 5 SLIDES  EXTENDING TO THE INKED DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 20 OF 20 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Several foci are highly suspicious for lymphatic invasion  Dr  Koerner agrees with the interpretation of blood vascular invasion  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast and axillary dissection  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable 1 5cm nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail is attached to the main specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  tan white stellate nodule extending to approximately REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm of the deep resection margin  Further sectioning reveals the remainder of the breast to be composed of predominantly fibrous  tan rubbery tissue intermixed with unremarkable adipose tissue  A representative section of the firm mass and deep resection margin is submitted in cassette A  Representative sections of the remainder of the mass are submitted in cassettes B through E  Representative sections of unremarkable parenchyma are submitted entirely in cassette F  The axillary tail is sectioned to reveal multiple rubbery tan pink lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes G through M  The nipple is trisected and submitted entirely in cassette N  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMBULATORY GEN SURG   ACC 457 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  and AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
