Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Paula Arnell  M D  Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  DCIS on core  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES RADIAL SCARS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  EXTENSIVE  BLUNT DUCT AND NODULAR ADENOSIS  PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Scattered foci involving 5 of 10 blocks and spanning at least 0 9cm  Grade  REMOVED_DATE Calcifications  In the carcinoma in situ and in benign changes  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 1cm from the superior margin of the specimen focally and extends to 0 12cm from the posterior margin of the specimen focally  Stains for receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Note  The ductal carcinoma in situ extensively involves sclerosing adenosis  distortion of the in situ carcinoma component by the adenosis makes evaluation for invasion difficult  No definite stromal invasion is identified  Immunohistochemical stains for myoepithelial markers  p63  calponin  and myosin  performed on multiple blocks confirm the presence of myoepithelial cells around the involved ducts and lobules  supporting the in situ nature of the proliferation in these foci  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SCLEROSING AND NODULAR ADENOSIS  NO DEFINITE IN SITU OR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  EXTENSIVE SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  NO DEFINITE IN SITU OR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm yellow white irregular fibrofatty tissue with a short stitch designating superior  and a long stitch designating lateral and a localization wire  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x0 7 x 0 6cm tan white ovoid well circumscribed rubbery nodule abutting the superior margin  0 3cm from the anterior margin  1 2cm to both the posterior and medial margins  and greater than 1 5cm of the remaining two margins  At 0 6cm from this nodule there is an ovoid tan granular area  0 6cm from both the superior and anterior margins  0 4cm from the posterior margin and  1 5cm from the remaining margins  0 7cm inferior from this area there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan ovoid nodule which comes within 0 8cm of both the anterior and inferior margins  1 0cm from the posterior margin  15 cm from the superior margin  and  1 5cm from the remaining two margins  The remainder of the cut surface consists of yellow lobulated adipose tissue with focally yellow  hemorrhagic chalky areas  admixed with white dense fibrous tissue  Representatives sections are submitted sequentially from medial to lateral in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Yellow chalky area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Granular area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Third nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral sections  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast superior half of cavity  