tibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm fibroadipose tissue with indicating wire  The specimen is inked as follows  black superior  red inferior  blue lateral  green medial  yellow deep  The specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  white area of irregular borders that is 0 5cm from closest  inferior  red  margin and 1 0cm from the superior  black  margin  The specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes A I  with firm area in cassettes C  D and E  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  with no designation as to site  are three portions of adipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Sectioning reveals two lymph nodes  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Each lymph node is bisected and entirely submitted  the smaller lymph node in cassette J  and the larger lymph nodes in K L  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  with no designation as to site  is a REMOVE