RCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  The ductal carcinoma in situ forms a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm mass lesion  GRADE  2  CALCIFICATIONS  In the carcinoma in situ and in benign changes  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Focally present at and broadly  0 1cm from the inferior margin  ductal carcinoma in situ also extends to 0 1cm from the anterior margin in one focus  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Will be attempted on the limited amount of intralymphatic tumor  See also  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SPANNING ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM AND PRESENT  0 2 CM FROM THE NEW MARGIN  2  FOCAL INTRALYMPHATIC TUMOR  SEE NOTE  1 ABOVE  3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  2  Immunostains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and p63 were examined  BREAST  RIGHT  POSTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  FOCAL FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimens were inked and microscopically evaluated  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in a single container   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 1cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with 2 needle localization wires in place  which has been oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  The long axis runs medial to lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green  inferior   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm lobulated  firm  white mass adjacent to needle localization wire  2  which is located 0 9cm from the medial margin  2 4cm from the lateral margin  1 7cm from the posterior margin  1 8cm from the superior margin  0 1cm from the anterior margin and abutting the inferior margin  There is 