hemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm overlying skin ellipse with a well healed 5 0cm long scar   The specimen has two stitches  the short stitch marking presumably the superior border and the long stitch marking the lateral end of the specimen   The specimen is inked black  the superior surface double inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from laterally to medially to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm biopsy cavity with indurated white borders up to 0 3cm in thickness  with fibrous strands extending to the deep and inferior margins  Section Code  A  lateral wall and biopsy cavity  B C D  representative sections of biopsy cavity   B and C are anterior and posterior extent of the specimen   E  lateral end of the biopsy cavity  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of yellow fibroadipose tissue  containing multiple lymph nodes up to 2 0cm in diameter  Representative sections of each node are submitted in cassettes F through H  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLARY  RIGHT  , Unchecked.
