Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 10 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  FEW SCATTERED CELLS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE  SPANNING ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION  OCCUPYING THREE OF EIGHT SECTIONS  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN  AND HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear negative for invasive carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins contain only a few invasive carcinoma cells  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a hemorrhagic but otherwise unremarkable piece of breast with localizing needle in place  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The entire specimen submitted in cassettes A through H  with areas corresponding to microcalcifcations in cassettes A through D  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  NO AREAS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
