Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 25 CLINICAL DATA  Patient presents with infiltrating ductal carcinoma in the tail of the breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 2 3   PRESENT AT SEVERAL DEEP  POSTERIOR  RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE     BIOPSY SITE WITH FIBROSIS  GRANULATION TISSUE  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  NOTE  Lymphatic invasion is present  No in situ carcinoma is identified in this specimen  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT   METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IS PRESENT IN 4 OF 21 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast short stitch superior  long lateral  is a 38 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm right breast lumpectomy specimen oriented with superior and lateral stitches  The specimen is partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm skin ellipse with a central 2 8cm well healed scar running along the long axis of the ellipse  there is no areola  There is no axillary tail on the specimen  The deep resection margin is a smooth plain  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a prior REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm cystic biopsy cavity filled with red tan groumous material  and surrounded by a rim of intense fibrosis and semi firm sulphur yellow discoloration  The biopsy site is inferior to the skin ellipse  and abuts the inferior resection margin  The biopsy site comes to within 0 1cm of the superior margin  0 4cm of the deep inked margin  0 6cm of the lateral margin  and 1 5cm of the medial margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of mature  lobular  yellow  adipose tissue with intercolating fibrous bands  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary contents  is a 36 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of tan yellow  lobulated  fibroadipose tissue which is explored for lymph nodes  Lymph nodes are identified  Summary of sections  A G  Biopsy site with skin  superior  in yellow   inferior  deep  from medial to lateral H M  Biopsy site with inferior  in yellow   deep  from medial to lateral N  Medial  en face O  Lateral  en face P S  Lymph nodes Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 12 13 CLINICAL DATA  70 y o  female with right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  CONSISTENT WITH EXTRANODAL MARGINAL ZONE B CELL LYMPHOMA  NOTE  Sections show a large mass lesion composed of a dense  diffuse to vaguely nodular  rather monotonous infiltrate of small lymphoid cells with slightly irregular nuclei with a small amount of clear cytoplasm  with scattered plasma cells and rare small aggregates of follicle center cells  The infiltrate abuts on the margin  The histologic features are consistent with marginal zone B cell lymphoma  and immunohistochemical studies support this interpretation  see addendum   Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 08                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibodies to immunoglobulin light chains there is polytypic staining of many plasma cells  With antibodies to B lineage antigen s    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  staining reveals extensive networks of dendritic cells  With antibodies to T lineage associated antigen s    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of small cells scattered within the tissue  Lymphocytes in rare aggregates are also positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   consistent with residual follicle centers  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results support the diagnosis of extranodal marginal zone B cell lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm predominantly yellow lobulated fibrofatty portion of unoriented breast notable for 2 wires flanking a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm slightly firm area  The specimen is black inked bivalved to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm pink gray firm ill defined area and the remainder predominantly yellow lobulated fatty parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted  SECTION CODES  A C  The entire ill defined pink area  D   Unremarkable parenchyma  Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
